# Embedded UI build assets (regenerated by npm run build)
internal/server/ui_dist/assets/
# index.html/vite.svg stay tracked (go:embed all:ui_dist in internal/server/spa.go
# needs this dir non-empty on a fresh clone before any frontend build runs) but are
# marked --skip-worktree so a local `npm run build`'s regenerated index.html doesn't
# show as dirty. To pick up a real upstream change to either file: run
# `git update-index --no-skip-worktree internal/server/ui_dist/index.html
# internal/server/ui_dist/vite.svg`, pull, then re-apply --skip-worktree.

# Scratch artifact-tool output (session-local, not build output)
/data/artifacts/

# Local exports
/exports/

# Vendored skill packages (internal/skillvendor, TASKS/skills/03/05) --
# content-addressed install output, not source. Was incidentally caught by
# the bare `vendor/` rule above (the default root is data/skills/vendor/),
# but that's a coincidence of the current directory name, not a deliberate
# ignore -- listed explicitly so it stays ignored regardless.
/data/skills/

# Plugins
/plugins/

# Badger coordination store (runtime data)
/coordination/

# Agent state (managed by services)
.agentrc/state/
.agentrc/.session-unclean.flag
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
worktrees/
/nanite

# Vite TS-config compile shims (transient)
ui/vite.config.ts.timestamp-*.js

# Visual brainstorming companion sessions
.superpowers/

# Audit evidence — REPORT.md cites these files by path as the backing evidence
# for every finding. The global *.log / *.out ignores would otherwise silently
# drop the entire evidence chain (21 of 29 files), leaving the citations
# dangling. This output cannot be regenerated: it was measured against a
# working tree at the audited commit that no longer exists.
!docs/audits/**/raw/*.log
!docs/audits/**/raw/*.out
!docs/audits/**/raw-*/*.log
!docs/audits/**/raw-*/*.out

# Python bytecode from scripts/ (py_compile, test runs)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Personal per-machine Claude Code settings — never tracked
.claude/settings.local.json
